    "body": "## Goal\nRedesign the MRT Supplier homepage to improve first-5-second clarity, visual impact, and RFQ conversion while preserving SEO and analytics behavior.\n\n## Target audiences\n1. End users / factories / procurement\n2. Maintenance technicians / service teams\n3. Provincial shops / spare-parts resellers\n\n## Growth objectives\n- Make the value proposition immediately clear.\n- Increase Search -> Product View -> RFQ progression.\n- Make RFQ, LINE, and product-detail submission obvious above the fold.\n- Present MRT Supplier as a nationwide industrial sourcing partner, not only a product catalog.\n- Preserve existing GA4/Meta event semantics and privacy controls.\n\n## Homepage structure\n1. High-impact industrial hero with dark image overlay.\n2. Strong Thai/English value proposition.\n3. Part Number / Cross Reference search above the fold.\n4. Primary CTA: Search products.\n5. Secondary CTA: Request Quote.\n6. LINE CTA for sending Part No. / product photos.\n7. Trust/value strip: product catalog, cross-reference support, bulk RFQ, nationwide support.\n8. \"Who we serve\" cards for End User / Maintenance / Provincial Reseller.\n9. Existing workflow, brands, categories, Why MRT, and final RFQ CTA retained but tightened.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Desktop + mobile responsive.\n- No new direct Meta Pixel/browser SDK calls.\n- Existing Search/RFQ/LINE tracking components retained where possible.\n- No change to RFQ submission event semantics.\n- No external PII added to analytics.\n- LINE OA must use https://lin.ee/PsQGAuu.\n- Customer-facing email remains sales@mrtsupplier.com.\n- No unsupported claims such as authorized distributor or guaranteed compatibility.\n- No fake testimonials, stock claims, delivery promises, or product counts beyond verified catalog count.\n- Build/lint/typecheck must pass.\n- Homepage metadata/canonical/hreflang remain valid.\n- Review via PR before production merge.",
